OPEN QUESTIONS  —  these are unresolved, and they are recorded here rather than assumed
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  (a) WHICH JUCE LICENCE. Not elected. JUCE's terms change between major versions and
      must be read at https://juce.com — do not rely on this file, or on any figure
      quoted elsewhere in this repository, for them.

  (b) `JUCE_DISPLAY_SPLASH_SCREEN=0` IS SET (native/audio-engine/CMakeLists.txt).
      Disabling JUCE's splash screen is a LICENCE-GATED act: it is permitted under the
      AGPL option and under paid tiers, and historically NOT under JUCE's free tier,
      which required the splash to be shown. This flag was set for engineering reasons
      (the addon is headless and has no window to draw one in) with no licence decision
      behind it. It must be reconciled with whichever tier is chosen.

  (c) THE LGPL STATIC-LINK RELINKING OBLIGATION for libspatialaudio (see above).

  (d) ARTLUX'S OWN LICENCE. There is no LICENSE file, so the work is "all rights
      reserved" by default. That is coherent for a private research project. It is NOT
      coherent with electing JUCE's AGPL option, which would require this application to
      be offered under AGPL-compatible terms when distributed.

  (e) DISTRIBUTION IS ALREADY WIRED. `package.json`'s `extraResources` ships
      `audio-engine.node` into every installer, and pushing a `v*` tag runs a CI matrix
      that PUBLISHES A GITHUB RELEASE. Building and running locally raises none of the
      above. PUBLISHING A RELEASE raises all of it.

  ⚠ Nothing in this file is legal advice. It is an engineer's inventory of what is
